From af07d8cae02634031ef4b009303430e3a1f9389b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Showta Ishizaki <zakinko@snowrabbit.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 05:17:48 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] nfsd: pass NFSv4 ACLs through on filesystems that have
 them

nfsd knows only POSIX ACLs, and an NFSv4 client mount has none.  On a
re-export the ACL attribute is therefore reported as unsupported, although
both ends speak NFSv4 ACLs.  Before commit 5aa8fd9cea2e ("fs: add a new
SB_I_NOUMASK flag") a re-exported client looked as though it had POSIX ACLs,
and the attribute came back as an ACL made from the mode, without the
entries set on the server.

Where the filesystem has NFSv4 ACLs, read and write them without going
through POSIX ACLs, and report ACL_MODEL_NFS4 as the true form.  A name with
no local id is kept as a string; on a filesystem with POSIX ACLs it still
gets NFS4ERR_BADOWNER.

Serve the dacl and sacl attributes of NFSv4.1 where the filesystem has them.
RFC 8881 6.4.1 requires a request setting acl with either of them to fail
with NFS4ERR_ATTRNOTSUPP, and 6.2.1.1 limits the ACE types of each.

Signed-off-by: Showta Ishizaki <zakinko@snowrabbit.org>
